From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] am: GetTicketList lists the titles that have a ticket (Build
 129)

The eShop's "Redownloadable software" and "Downloaded titles" pages stayed
at 0 after buying a game from the eShop stand-in, although NIM had
imported its ticket into nand/dbs/ticket.db.

The eShop builds both pages from am GetNumTickets + GetTicketList (title
IDs with a ticket), leaves out what is installed, and only then asks the
shop for the titles' names (ninja titles/id_pair, never requested). Our
GetTicketList (from Citra/Azahar) had the ticket code under #ifdef
todotodo and wrote the installed-title list instead, while GetNumTickets
counted ticket files. So a bought title that isn't installed was never
in the list, and the count and the list described different things.

Both now use one list: every title with a ticket file first, then every
installed title without one (so programs that look for an installed
title's ticket still find it, as before), without duplicates.
GetTicketList also honours its start index now.
GetNumTickets logs both counts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
